[38;2;124;124;124mIn an associative algebra, $(xy)y^{-1} = x(yy^{-1}) = x \cdot 1 = x$. The Jordan[0m[38;2;124;124;124malgebra is not associative, so this chain of equalities breaks down. My [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcounterexample shows it concretely.[0m

